    "knowledge_point": "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial",
    "problem": "Solve the inequality $3x\\cdot {5}^{x+6}-{5}^{x+6}<8\\cdot {5}^{x+6}.$",
    "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x\\cdot {5}^{x+6}-{5}^{x+6} & <8\\cdot {5}^{x+6} \\\\ 3x\\cdot {5}^{x+6}-{5}^{x+6}-8\\cdot {5}^{x+6} & <0 \\\\ (3x-1-8){5}^{x+6} & <0 \\\\ (3x-9){5}^{x+6} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${5}^{x+6}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-9 & <0 \\\\ 3x & <9 \\\\ x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the inequality above is $x<3.$",
